{#
  src/indicators/index.njk — the indicator hub

  The parent of the per-record /indicators/{id}/ pages built by
  indicator-page.njk, and the one place that states the site-wide total.

  It exists because no single search returns everything. iocIndex assigns each
  record an `area` and three different pages search those areas, for reasons
  documented in src/_data/iocIndex.js — an on-chain contract and a compromised
  repository answer different questions from an operator's email address. That
  split is right, but it left the full figure with nowhere to live, so the
  homepage quoted the largest area as though it were the whole index.

  Every count here is derived from iocIndex.totals. Do not type one in.
#}
<section>
  <h1>Indicators</h1>
  <p>
    This site holds {{ iocIndex.totals.all | thousands }} indicators, each with
    its own page, citation and source passage. They are searched from several
    places because each kind answers a different question.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <ul class="card-grid cluster-grid">
    <li class="card"><a class="cluster-card__link" href="/remote-workers/"><span class="cluster-card__name">Remote Workers</span><span class="cluster-card__count"><span class="count-figure">{{ iocIndex.totals.remote_workers | thousands }}</span> indicators</span><span class="cluster-card__body">Indicators for the operators themselves: email addresses, GitHub and LinkedIn accounts, packages, wallets, malware hashes and infrastructure reported in connection with DPRK remote IT-worker operations and the Contagious Interview lures run alongside them.</span></a></li>
    <li class="card"><a class="cluster-card__link" href="/#actor-cluster-taxonomy"><span class="cluster-card__name">Espionage clusters</span><span class="cluster-card__count"><span class="count-figure">{{ iocIndex.totals.espionage | thousands }}</span> indicators</span><span class="cluster-card__body">Intrusion and heist indicators for the named DPRK APT clusters -- Lazarus Group, Kimsuky, APT37, Konni, APT38, Andariel and Moonstone Sleet. These answer a different question from the remote-worker identities they were filed beside, so they are grouped and searched on each cluster's own page.</span></a></li>
    <li class="card"><a class="cluster-card__link" href="/etherhiding/"><span class="cluster-card__name">EtherHiding Tracker</span><span class="cluster-card__count"><span class="count-figure">{{ iocIndex.totals.etherhiding | thousands }}</span> indicators</span><span class="cluster-card__body">On-chain command-and-control infrastructure: the smart contracts and wallet addresses used to stage payloads on public blockchains, tracked separately because they are infrastructure rather than identities.</span></a></li>
    <li class="card"><a class="cluster-card__link" href="/repo-scanner/?cluster=PolinRider#repository-indicators"><span class="cluster-card__name">PolinRider Repositories</span><span class="cluster-card__count"><span class="count-figure">{{ iocIndex.totals.polinrider | thousands }}</span> indicators</span><span class="cluster-card__body">Repositories the PolinRider campaign compromised. These name projects that were attacked rather than the people who ran the attack, which is why they are kept out of the remote-worker index and searched from the repo scanner instead.</span></a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Browsing without searching</h2>
  <p>
    Every indicator is also laid out as plain pages of links, by type;
    <a href="/indicators/browse/">Browse indicators</a> lists every page.
  </p>
  {# Type and count only. The page-number links for each run live on
     /indicators/browse/, one click on, which keeps every indicator page within
     four clicks of the home page without a row of bare numbers here. #}
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="results-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Indicators</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for entry in iocIndex.indicator_browse_types %}
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.kind.plural }}</a></th>
          <td>{{ entry.total | thousands }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h2>Reading an indicator page</h2>
  <p>
    Each page at <code>/indicators/&lt;id&gt;/</code> lists every source that
    reported the value and what it said. Downloads are on
    <a href="/data/">Data and downloads</a>.
  </p>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Disclaimer",
    preset: "not-proof",
    body: 'Compromised packages and repositories name victims. See the <a href="/sources/#sourcing-methodology">sourcing methodology</a>.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}
</section>
